Hi Ed,

The confusion is because you have an "apples to oranges" comparison 
here.  There are 390 unique KEGG IDs in the DB.  That means that there 
are only 390 KEGG names for those pathways.  However, those pathway IDs 
are matched up to over 3000 different external gene IDs which is why the 
second mapping is so much larger.  You can learn more about the 
different mappings by reading their manual pages like this:

help("KEGGPATHID2NAME")

help("KEGGPATHID2EXTID")


   Marc


 >


