Hi Burkhard,

Well, that all looks OK. So the next likely culprit is affylmGUI itself. 
Since you are not getting the gene symbols, it would be reasonable to 
assume that affylmGUI is trying to download and install the correct 
annotation package.

You don't say what chip data you are analyzing, so I can't give much 
more than a generalized pointer. If it is an old-school 3'-biased chip 
(like the HG-U133 plus 2 chip), then you can usually get really close to 
the right name by just reducing to lower case and removing all 
punctuation, then adding a .db, so e.g, hgu133plus2.db is the annotation 
package. If you are using a Gene ST package, then you want to do the 
same, but add transcriptcluster.db. So e.g., the HuGene 1.0 ST chip 
annotation package is the hugene10sttranscriptcluster.db.

So try installing the correct annotation package first, then do your 
analysis. See if that helps.

Best,

Jim



